  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -42,6 +42,27 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark grabs your ID at 3 am, goes to Waffle House, and insults people.\n \n+* Capture start fails when file set enabled and file extension not supplied if directory contains a period. wsbuglink:14614[].\n+* Cannot drag and move custom filter buttons in toolbar. wsbuglink:19447[].\n+* Not equal won't work when used with wlan.addr. wsbuglink:19449[].\n+* sshdump fails to connect with private key (ssh-rsa) wsbuglink:19510[].\n+* ChmodBPF installation fails on macOS Sonoma 14.1.2. wsbuglink:19527[].\n+* Windows installers should check for Windows 8.1. wsbuglink:19569[].\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2024-01-05-7725.pcap. wsbuglink:19570[].\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2024-01-06-7734.pcap. wsbuglink:19578[].\n+* Incorrect recursion depth assert failure when dissecting a legitimate GOOSE message. wsbuglink:19580[].\n+* OPC UA - large read request is reported as malformed in 4.2.1 but not in 4.0.12. wsbuglink:19581[].\n+* TFTP dissector bug type listed as netscii instead of netascii doesn't show all TFTP packets including TFTP blocks. wsbuglink:19589[].\n+* SMB1 replies from LAN Drive app only show up as NBSS Continuation Message. wsbuglink:19593[].\n+* ciscodump - older SSH key exchange algorithms not supported. wsbuglink:19594[].\n+* Problem decoding LAPB/X.25/FTAM after adding X.75 decoding. wsbuglink:19595[].\n+* Wireshark Filter not working. wsbuglink:19604[].\n+* CFLOW: failure to decode 0 length data fields of IPFIX variable length data types. wsbuglink:19605[].\n+* Copy ...as Printable Text Feature Missing in 4.1/4.2. wsbuglink:19607[].\n+* Export Objects - HTTP is missing some HTTP/2 files in a two-pass analysis. wsbuglink:19609[].\n+* ASAM-CMP Plugin: Malformed message, length mismatch if vendor defined data of status messages has odd length. wsbuglink:19626[].\n+* OSS-Fuzz 66561: wireshark:fuzzshark_ip_proto-udp: Null-dereference READ in wmem_map_lookup. wsbuglink:19642[].\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n There are no new or updated features in this release.\n@@ -63,15 +84,65 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.2.2.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+ASAM CMP\n+CAN\n+CFLOW\n+CMIP\n+CMP\n+DAP\n+DICOM\n+DISP\n+E2AP\n+GLOW\n+GOOSE\n+GTP\n+GTPv2\n+H.225\n+H.245\n+H.248\n+HTTP2\n+IEEE 1609.2\n+IEEE 1722\n+IPv4\n+IPv6\n+ISO 15765\n+ISUP\n+ITS\n+Kerberos\n+LDAP\n+MMS\n+NBT\n+openSAFETY\n+NRUP\n+P22\n+P7\n+PARLAY\n+RTMPT\n+RTP\n+SCSI\n+SOME/IP\n+T.38\n+TCP\n+TECMP\n+TFTP\n+WOW\n+X11\n+X.509if\n+X.509sat\n+X.75\n+Z39.50\n+ZigBee Green Power\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// [commaize]\n-// --\n-// --\n+[commaize]\n+--\n+pcap\n+pcapng\n+--\n \n // === New and Updated Capture Interfaces support\n \n",
